---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { aff } from "../data/affiliates";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="eSIM for Georgia — city vs mountains | ArriveGE"
  description="Buy a Georgia eSIM before your flight. Choose a city plan for Tbilisi and Batumi, or mountain coverage for Kazbegi and the Military Highway."
  nextHref="/tbilisi-airport-transfer"
  nextLabel="airport transfer"
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="page-hero-inner" data-reveal>
      <p class="section-kicker">Buy before takeoff</p>
      <h1>eSIM for Georgia</h1>
      <p>
        Install at home on Wi‑Fi. When you land in Tbilisi, maps and Bolt work without hunting a SIM kiosk.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main class="section content-grid">
    <article class="prose" data-reveal>
      <h2>Pick by route, not by “unlimited”</h2>
      <p>
        Georgia’s networks are not equal outside the cities. Magti holds the Military Highway and many mountain villages
        better. City-focused plans are fine for Tbilisi and Batumi only.
      </p>

      <table class="compare">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Your trip</th>
            <th>What to buy</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Tbilisi / Batumi only</td>
            <td>City eSIM — maps, chat, rideshare</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Kazbegi, Svaneti, Military Highway</td>
            <td>Mountain eSIM on Magti-class coverage</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Need local calls / SMS</td>
            <td>Plan that includes minutes, not data-only</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>Install checklist</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Buy and install before boarding, on stable Wi‑Fi.</li>
        <li>Turn on data roaming only for the eSIM line.</li>
        <li>Keep your home SIM as secondary so banking SMS still arrive if needed.</li>
        <li>Open the operator page on purchase day — prices and GB change.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <aside class="action-panel" data-reveal>
      <h2>Book connectivity</h2>
      <p>Affiliate links. Commission if you buy through them. Compare the live plan before checkout.</p>
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href={aff("esimCity")} target="_blank" rel="noopener sponsored noreferrer"
        >City eSIM (Tbilisi / Batumi)</a
      >
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={aff("esimMountains")} target="_blank" rel="noopener sponsored noreferrer"
        >Mountain eSIM (Kazbegi+)</a
      >
      <p class="disclaimer">
        We may earn a commission. This is not a guarantee of coverage on every trail — check the network listed on the
        plan page.
      </p>
    </aside>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
